From Mrs. Edna Sheridan:
<p>
Was a seamstress, working only on the trim(lace, beads etc?) for FINE dresses. Sounds like she was the stereotypical mother-in-law! Very snotty, "had a mouth" A story - when Thomas and Edna were first married, a friend had taught her how to crochet, so she made a simple table runner(?) as her first project. Well, Tom's parents lived on one end of the block and Edna's mother lived on the other, so every night the in-laws would be on their walk and stop by in the evening. Edna was proud of what she made and so was Tom, so when Anastasia made her nightly visit he took his mother over to show off the talents of his new wife. Anastasia apparently lifted up a corner of the runner, took one look and merely said "dust collector" and walked away!

